== Notes ==
* {{dlc|na}} Exiting the Black Market through the beam of light in {{s|Chest}} or {{s|Dark Room}} causes the floor to restart (in a similar fashion to {{i|Forget Me Now}}), as there are no floors further than these two. This can come in handy to gather a lot of items. The same applies to {{R|I AM ERROR}}.
** {{dlc|a}} Black Markets and {{R|I AM ERROR}} can no longer be accessed in Chest or Dark Room.
*** {{dlc|r}} {{R|I AM ERROR}} rooms can be accessed by exiting a {{r|Crawl Space}} in an unintended direction.
* {{dlc+|a+}} Black Markets and {{R|I AM ERROR}} can be found in {{s|The Void}}. Using the trapdoor causes the floor to restart (in a similar fashion to {{i|Forget Me Now}}).{{dlc-}}
** {{dlc|a+}} Players can no longer access the Black Market through the wall glitch. However, it is still possible to access the Black Market using the glitch via special circumstances including having Ipecac and The Inner Eye.
* {{C|The Lost}} can take items from the Black Market for free, just like with regular devil deals.
** {{dlc|r}} The Lost can take only one item from each selection of items. When an item is taken, the others disappear.
** {{dlc|r}} If a Black Market is found in the [[Mirrored World]] and is populated using a {{M|Shop Restock Machine}}, it will follow the rules of the non-mirrored character. Despite playing as The Lost in this area, multiple items can be purchased, and health will be deducted from the non-mirrored character, possibly resulting in death.
* {{dlc|r}} When playing as {{C|Keeper}}, the items are sold for money instead, making it no different from a regular Shop.
* {{dlc|r}} When two crawl spaces lead to a Black Market in the same floor, they lead to the same Black Market.
* {{dlc|r}} During the [[Ascent]], crawlspaces with Black Markets lead to an {{R|I AM ERROR}} room instead.

== Trivia ==
* In the game files, every Black Market room is named "# - The Black Market (Racist Placeholder) (copy)", which can be seen with the "Debug 5" command.

